----
== Nothing is true. Everything is permitted. --Naked Lunch

* Something you likely didn't know about YAML…

* Who has heard of YAML's "Norway Problem"?
    no: Det er ikke noe problem!

* There is no problem! (since 2009, YAML 1.2)
  * https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/#103-core-schema
  * "YAML Schema" being renamed to "YAML Rules"

* YAML has some recommended Rules
  * Mostly for YAML interchange (rare use case)
  * These were only intended as recommendations

* YAML wants you to make up your own Rules!

----
== How YAML is processed: The Dump/Load Stack

  https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/#31-processes

      Loader             Data State               Dumper
=============================================================
                     (Native Data Objects)
 Constructor                                      Representer
                  (YAML Representation Graph)
    Resolver                                      Desolver
                       (YAML Node Graph)
    Composer                                      Serializer
                      (YAML Event Stream)
      Parser                                      Emitter
                      (YAML Token Stream)
     Scanner
                    (YAML Character Stream)
      Reader                                      Writer
                 (YAML String or File Handle)

----
== Implicit Tagging

* YAML has a "tag" syntax (!!bool !foo)
  * A per node annotation word
  * Rarely used in real world YAML files

* YAML's Load "implicitly tags" every node internally
  * Done by the "Resolver" stage
  * Tagged accourding to "YAML Rules"

* A tag is a key to a "Constructor" function
  * Turn a YAML "node" into a native value

  What if you could "Change the Rules"?!

----
== No is not false. Everything is configurable. --Ingy döt Net

* You were supposed to Make Your Own Rules!
* PyYAML supports this. Others to a degree.
* But only by using complicated code (not portable)

* Customizing YAML should be as easy as using YAML
* Make Your Own DSL Languages in YAML
  * YAMLScript, YAMLSchema are YAML DSLs

