== The go-yaml CLI

The yaml/go-yaml project has a CLI called: 'go-yaml'

# Some example YAML:

    a: [ok, 1, 2.0, true, no, null] # implicits

https://play.yaml.com/?show=gdhflLnJPpxHUrsS#YTogW29rLCAxLCAyLjAsIHRydWUsIG51bGxdICMgaW1wbGljaXRz

> source <(curl -sL in-1.cc) go-yaml
$ go-yaml --help

$ <<<'a: [ok, 1, 2.0, true, no, null] # implicits' go-yaml -J
$ <<<'a: [ok, 1, 2.0, true, no, null] # implicits' go-yaml -Y
$ <<<'a: [ok, 1, 2.0, true, no, null] # implicits' go-yaml -N

----
== Introducing 'in-1' and Makes

* https://in-1.cc
  * https://in-1.cc/installables

* Makes auto-installs many deps for Makefiles
  * https://github.com/makeplus/makes

* Quickly Install Languages and Tools

* Everything in this talk can be installed

> source <(curl -sL in-1.cc) in-1
> in-1 ys yaml ysd go-yaml gloat glj

* Enables tab completion and man pages too!

----
== Introducing YAMLScript

* Aka YS (wise)

* YS is dynamic transform language for YAML
* Also a very complete programming language

* All YS is 100% valid YAML

* Existing YAML files evaluate as expected

> in-1 ys
$ <<<'say: "Hello, $(ENV.USER)!"' ys - -J
$ <<<$'!ys-0\nsay: "Hello, $(ENV.USER)!"' ys -
$ ys -e 'say: "Hello, $(ENV.USER)!"'

* A simple YS program
$ vim hello.ys
$ ys hello.ys

----
== How YS Works

* YS compiles to Clojure code
* Then it is evaluated

$ ys -c hello.ys

# Normal YAML data is still code:
$ vim normal-data.yaml
$ ys -c normal-data.yaml
$ ys -J normal-data.yaml

# !ys-0 tag makes it dynamic:
$ vim -O dynamic-data.yaml normal-data.yaml
$ ys -c dynamic-data.yaml
$ ys -J dynamic-data.yaml

----
== From Clojure to Glojure

* Clojure is a Lisp that compiles to JVM bytecode (Java)
* GraalVM (`native-image` compiler) made it fast
  * JVM bytecode -> Native

* YS recently moved to Glojure
* Glojure is a Clojure Dialect hosted on Go
  * Turns Clojure (and YS) into Go code

* Go is a better foundation for YAML
  * Kubernetes and friends
  * Go is fast and (cross-)compiles to so many places

* I don't like writing Go code…
+  * But I love compiling to Go code!

----
== YS → Glojure → Go → Everywhere!

* YS ships binary releases for more platforms now
  * Intel/ARM Linux/Mac/Windows/FreeBSD/Wasm
  * https://github.com/yaml/yamlscript/releases/tag/0.3.4

  Compile to binary (linux ELF):
> ys --to=bin hello.ys
$ file hello
$ time ./hello

  Cross compile to macOS Arm64:
> ys --to=bin,darwin/arm64 hello.ys
$ file hello
$ time ./hello

  Compile to Go code
$ ys -Tgo hello.ys

  Compile to browser Wasm, HTML wrapper and serve:
> ys -Tjs,html,serve hello.ys

----
== Introducing Gloat

* Gloat is an automation tool for Glojure

* YS → Clojure
  * → Go files
    * and Go build dirs
* Go files →
  * → Native Binaries
  * → Shared librari
  * → Wasm

* https://gloathub.org

> in-1 gloat
$ gloat --help

----
== The YS compiler is a special YAML Loader

* With some intense YAML Rules!

* Typical YAML loaders load to nodes or native
  * YS loads to a Clojure AST!
  * The AST trivially renders to Clojure

$ cat hello.ys
$ ys hello.ys
$ ys -c hello.ys
$ ys -c -d hello.ys  # The sausage factory!

